The `serve-dev.js` script uses Node.js to create an HTTP server that serves files from the `out/html` directory. It sets up proper MIME types and includes headers to disable caching. The server listens on port 8765 and ensures that index.html is served when the root path is requested. This setup allows for local development without relying on file:// protocol caching issues.

